wildos-settings (0.1.4) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Sign-in options has a saved passwords dialog, opened from that
    notification (--page signin-wallet): it checks your password, keeps the
    automatic sign-in key, and moves a wallet with another password to your
    account password.

 -- Wild OS Developers <dev@wildos.io>  Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0000

wildos-settings (0.1.3) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Changing your password works again: it goes through wildos-wallet-keys
    instead of passwd, and a password the rules turn down says why.

 -- Wild OS Developers <dev@wildos.io>  Tue, 10 Nov 2026 13:00:00 +0000

wildos-settings (0.1.2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Turning on automatic sign-in asks for your password, so your saved
    passwords (KWallet) open by themselves at each start. Turning it off,
    or removing the account, removes the key the system kept for it.
  * Changing your password moves your saved passwords to the new password,
    so they keep opening when you sign in, and refreshes the kept key.

 -- Wild OS Developers <dev@wildos.io>  Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000

wildos-settings (0.1.1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Accessibility has Outline windows, Stronger text on glass and Blur windows
    in the background, with a blur strength and a choice to blur the desktop
    too.
  * wildos-auto-theme puts on the solid Plasma style while stronger text on
    glass is on.

 -- Wild OS Developers <dev@wildos.io>  Tue, 10 Nov 2026 08:10:42 +0000

